00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.000
they don't have, they cannot work, they don't have a work permit.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.000
This is the next category.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:08.000
But the Zakat must be given on, on your net income, 2.5%, immediately.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:17.000
When you read the Quran, we see that Zakat and Salat, Salat, NAMAZ and Zakat are together, always, as if they are a daily process.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.000
In fact, the very, the first, first page of the Quran.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.000
In Sura Al-Baqarah, Sura number 2, not the first page, but the second page.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.000
Definition of the Righteous

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:43.000
They observe the Contact Prayers, and spend from our provisions to them, which is these two, Salat and Zakat.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Right at the beginning of the Quran, these two points are mentioned.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:53.000
These are the minimum, number one and two are minimum sets.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:58.000
By the way, the Zakat, as it is practiced in the Muslim world is not, it doesn't make sense.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Because if you have a theoretical calculation of something, let's say you have 40 million dollars, and, in the savings,

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:13.000
you give 2.5% of that, a million dollars.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:18.000
