Maybe, you also heard this from the Arthritis Foundation.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:21.000
It says "do not stay in, in the same position, sit in the same position for a long time."

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:25.000
Some truck driver was asking "what do I do? I have arthritis."

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:30.000
And they said "every few hours you must get out and stretch."

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:38.000
Now, when we go to sleep and we, we sit like that, the joints become stiff. They need to be lubricated.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:47.000
So, God does not want to bother us and annoy us by asking us to get up before sunrise every day.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:49.000
He doesn't need us to do that.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.000
We need it.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.000
So, if we do the Morning Prayer...

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:59.000
I'm sorry I (unintelligible), but this is the physical part of it.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.000
If you get up and lubricate your joints, and you will not have arthritis when you grow up, (unintelligible).

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:12.000
The spiritual part of it is you can measure the degree of your development.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:19.000
Because as you become strong, you, not the body, you become strong, your body will become obedient to you.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.000
So, you can measure if, if you wake up...

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:27.000
If you cannot wake up at all in the morning, you are in bad shape.

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:36.000
You cannot tell your body to get up for your own good, for the morning meal, the Morning Prayer before sunrise.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.000
Because there is a fight between you and your body every morning.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:48.000
If you, if you decide to do this, there comes tomorrow morning before sunrise and the body wants to sleep.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:54.000
But you need, you need to, to make it wake up.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:22:02.000
So, this struggle takes place and one of you wins, either you or your body.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:07.000
If the body wins, you continue to sleep. And you will continue to be weak.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:14.000
If you win, you will grow and you develop and the growth of the soul is very fast.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.000
Sura 17

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.000
It says "the growth..."

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:22.000
See, we grow until we're 5 feet or 6 feet tall.

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:27.000
But the soul grows until it is bigger than San Francisco, the soul, your soul.

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.000
So, the degree of growth is, the gain is fantastic.

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:38.000
It's not like, you know, we eat this food to grow and we're very limited in growth, the body is.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.000
But the soul grows immensely.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:46.000
So, if you succeed in, in forcing your body to get up before sunrise and do the Morning,

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:51.000
make contact with your Creator before sunrise, you grow a lot.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.000
So, at first, it will be difficult.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:23:05.000
But in a month or two, you will grow sufficiently that when you say to your body "get up and do the Morning Contact Prayer", it will get up grudgingly.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:11.000
And this will show you another, the degree of your growth.

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.000
You will be on your way.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:18.000
It will be very good but then even though your body is getting up grudgingly to do the Contact Prayer, it's very good.

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:21.000
Better than saying "no" and losing to your body.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:27.000
But gradually as you grow stronger, your body will become absolutely obedient to you.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
This will tell you how much growth you attained.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:36.000
There comes a time before sunrise to set the alarm. In fact, you will not need to set the alarm anymore.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.000
This is true. You will not need it.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:47.000
You will wake up your body at the right time before sunrise to get up to do the Contact Prayer.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:51.000
And your body obediently will, will start to enjoy.

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:56.000
And this will tell you at what degree, where you stand.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:02.000
And eventually, you will really enjoy. You will be enjoying the Morning Prayer.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:06.000
You will be very cheerful. Most people get up in the morning and have a long face.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:11.000
But you'll get up with a big smile every morning before sunrise.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:17.000
So, this will provide you with a yardstick as to the degree of your growth.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.000
Now, Fasting does the same thing.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Because first thing in the morning, your body wants breakfast.

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:33.000
And you issue a command to your body. "No, I'm not gonna eat or drink not until sunset."

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:35.000
And this will cause you to grow and develop.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
So, God designed these things.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:43.000
Zakat also (unintelligible) you're taking, not your money, but most people love very much, and you give it away.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:51.000
So, you can see that all these are designed for, for our benefit to make our souls grow and develop.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:52.000
These are gifts from God.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:56.000
And if you are fortunate to receive the gift, you will do these things.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.000
It seems like what it takes is a decision.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:05.000
You decide that you want to worship God alone.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:09.000
Then, God will give you these gifts and you'll be able to do it.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:13.000
So, your part is really very easy. All you need to do is a decision.

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:18.000
"I want to be redeemed. I want to be with God alone."

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:24.000
"I believe that Muhammad, Jesus, Mary, Hussein, Ali, none of them has any power."

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:26.000
"Only God has all power."

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:29.000
So, the question, this is all you need, a decision.

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:33.000
And God, you'll see that you do these things automatically.

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:46.000
The fourth minimum, we call it ZIKR (ذکر).

00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.000
I just wrote it ZIKR (ذکر).

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:58.000
But I have to explain it.

00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:01.000
In the Quran, there's a commandment, in the Quran, that's very important that says,

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.000
(33:41) يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ [33:41] O you who believe...

00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:07.000
(33:41) ٱذْكُرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ ذِكْرًۭا كَثِيرًۭا [33:41] ... remember GOD continuously.*

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:09.000
A lot. Frequently.

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:17.000
And this is not any ritual or anything that you perform. It's something that you do continuously.

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:22.000
You look at this view and say "Subhan Allah." God be glorified.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:27.000
You realize God's creation, the beauty that God created in the world.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.000
You look at the fruit.

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:30.000
Look how many flavors we have here.

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:34.000
When I say the word "orange", you think of a certain flavor.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:38.000
Then, I say "strawberry."

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:40.000
And you think of a certain flavor.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:46.000
Strawberry has a color, texture, taste, flavor, smell.

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:49.000
And these are all chemicals that God created in the strawberry.

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:51.000
There is peach.

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:54.000
(unintelligible)

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:57.000
So, when you look at this, you say, "Subhan Allah."

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:00.000
And God didn't have to do all this.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:02.000
But this is ZIKR (ذکر).

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:07.000
When we say "Subhan Allah", we think of God's creation and God's Greatness.

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:09.000
This is what we do with ZIKR (ذکر).

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:11.000
But let me start from the beginning.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:16.000
The minimum that you want to set for yourself is starts when you wake up in the morning.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:23.000
The first thing you must say in the morning must be the name of God, first thing you say.

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:30.000
In this country, most people start with a dirty word in the morning, every morning, when the alarm goes off.

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:35.000
You want to start with the name of God.

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:38.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:40.000
La Elaha Ella Allah

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:42.000
There is no god except the One God.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:49.000
It's gonna take you three or four months if you're not doing it already, it's gonna take you three or four months, at least, to get used to it.

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:53.000
The first thing you do when you open up your eyes.

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:54.000
This is ZIKR (ذکر).

00:27:56.000 --> 00:28:00.000
Because what you utter, the first thing you say in the morning, every morning, this is

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.000
what you'll utter when you get up on the Day of Resurrection.

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:08.000
The real life, the eternal life, that will determine your rank forever.

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:13.000
And you don't wanna utter a dirty word on the Day of Resurrection.

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:19.000
So, this is the first thing we do, and of course, we do the Morning Prayer.

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:28.000
There are certain commandments in the Quran, straightforward commandments, that you must do to carry out this, this gift.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:35.000
For example, in Sura 18, God says "Do not say, I will do anything without saying IN SHAA ALLAH", saying "God willing."

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:37.000
It says,

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:39.000
(18:23) لَا تَقُولَنَّ لِشَا۟ىْءٍ Do not say about anything

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:42.000
(18:23) إِنِّى فَاعِلٌ ذَٰلِكَ غَدًا I'm doing this tomorrow

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:45.000
(18:24) إِلَّآ أَن يَشَآءَ ٱللَّهُ without saying IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:53.000
You must never say "I'm gonna see you tomorrow" and that's it.

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:55.000
You must say "I'll see you tomorrow, God willing."

00:28:55.000 --> 00:29:04.000
Even when you work with Americans, or non-Muslims, at first, you'll be shy, they're (unintelligible) to say "what is this?"

00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:07.000
And they will say that. They'll be taken aback when you say "God willing",

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:13.000
but eventually, they will respect you, and they will get used to it, and you'll be carrying out your duty.

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:16.000
You're actually reminding the people of their Creator.

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Say "I'm gonna finish this at 6 o'clock, God willing.

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:24.000
And it must become a habit. Again, it'll take 3 or 4 months,

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:26.000
but this is a commandment in the Quran.

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:31.000
"Do not say, I will do anything without saying 'IN SHAA ALLAH.'"

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:39.000
The Quran gives you a commandment, also, that if you want to invoke protection for your children, for example,

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:43.000
or your car, or your property, you must say "Mã Shã Allãh."

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:46.000
This is Sura 18, also.

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:48.000
(unintelligible)

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:51.000
This man who lost his garden.

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:56.000
God says "if only when you entered your garden, you said 'Mã Shã Allãh.' The complete statement is

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.000
(18:39) مَا شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَا قُوَّةَ إِلَّا بِٱللَّهِ

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:01.000
you would not have lost your garden.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:11.000
So, this tells us that in order to invoke protection for your own children, your own property, your own car,

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:15.000
you say "Mã Shã Allãh." You start your car and starts like that, very nicely, you say "Mã Shã Allãh."

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:19.000
Now, before you start, say "Bismillah." (unintelligible)

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:22.000
This is what ZIKR (ذکر) is.

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:27.000
You must seek every chance to mention God.

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:35.000
This is because we came to the realization, and this is very important, that your god... who's your god?

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:37.000
Let me stop you and ask you a question. Don't answer me.

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:40.000
It's in your mind. In your mind.

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:43.000
In your mind, answer me. Who is your god?

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.000
So, every one of you is saying "my god is the Creator of the heavens and the earth."

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:51.000
And most of you are wrong.

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:56.000
Shocked, we were shocked when we came to this realization.

00:30:57.000 --> 00:31:02.000
Two times. When we came to this realization, and I was speaking and writing sermons.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:07.000
We were all shocked, because we examined ourselves as to who is our god.

00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:11.000
Because it turns out, when you study the Quran carefully, that your god

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:15.000
is whoever or whatever occupies your mind most of the day.

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:21.000
And we examined ourselves, and we found that the Creator of the heavens and the earth was not our god.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:27.000
We thought we were believers, and we thought our god was the Creator of the heavens and the earth.

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:34.000
And this would have been the, and this is the answer that the Quran gives, describing many people, who are headed, going, going to Hell.

00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:42.000
At the end of Sura 23, for example, "if you ask them, who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, and the Lord of the great dominion?"

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:54.000
(23:86) قُلْ مَن رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ ٱلسَّبْعِ وَرَبُّ ٱلْعَرْشِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ (23:87) سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ ۚ قُلْ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:55.000
Why are you...

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:56.000
[23:89] ... "Where did you go wrong?"

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:00.000
So, here, they are saying "God, the Lord of the heavens and the earth."

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:06.000
But you see, they are saying it with their mouth, and this is the answer with their mouth,

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:08.000
but they are preoccupied with other things.

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:15.000
Therefore, this is why the commandment to "remember constantly", is very important.

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:18.000
At least, 51% of the day.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:27.000
And it's very easy, I know you're thinking, "how can I come? I'm at work, I'm busy with the computer, and so on. How can I think of God?"

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:34.000
It's really very easy, because when you're go to the computer, you look, and you see somebody put a flower on the desk or something,

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:35.000
you see flowers on your desk.

00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:39.000
You look at the design of the flower, you say "Subhan Allah." God be glorified.

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:42.000
This will satisfy (unintelligible).

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:49.000
This is why it will interrupt your, your thinking and concentration of the world,

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.000
and you'll, you'll, you'll think of God.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:55.000
By the way, I'll go back to the Contact Prayers.

00:32:55.000 --> 00:33:01.000
The Five Contact Prayers go a long way, towards, this, remembering God.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:08.000
As a matter of fact, if you look at Sura 20, verse 14, God says,

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:10.000
[20:14] ... observe the Contact Prayers (Salat) to remember Me.

00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:13.000
(20:14) وَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ لِذِكْرِىٓ

00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:14.000
(unintelligible)

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:22.000
This is the reason, for giving you this gift, is to cause you to remember God, because it is not just the two minutes,

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:25.000
you know, we went back there and prayed the Afternoon Prayer, two minutes.

00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:32.000
It is not just those two minutes, that are counted in your favor, as credit for you.

00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:37.000
Two hours ago, we looked at the watch, and we said "oh, it's not the Afternoon Prayer yet."

00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:42.000
See, that's remembering God then, and this goes to the credit.

00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:48.000
And an hour later, we said "oh, is it time for the Afternoon Prayer? No, it is not."

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:56.000
So, you're thinking of God. What is the Afternoon Prayer? You're doing it, you're not doing it to get a salary, or to be paid.

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:58.000
You're doing it for God, and just thinking about it.

00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:05.000
So, the Five Prayers, when you go to sleep, you say "I hope I get up before sunrise tomorrow, to pray the Morning Prayer."

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.000
So, that, that is it.

00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:15.000
The Five Prayers every day, this is why the most important minimum gift for your soul is the Five Prayers.

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.000
They go a long way.

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:21.000
Soul's making the Creator of the heavens and the earth, your god,

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:24.000
and not your job, or your spouse, or your children, or your property.

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:27.000
These are the gods and are counted in the Quran.

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:36.000
The gods, that are counted in the Quran, include spouses, a man who worships his wife, instead God,

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:38.000
or a wife who worships her husband, instead of God.

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:45.000
Children, giving more attention to our children, than to God.

00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:48.000
These are also counted as gods. Sura 7.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:54.000
Sura 7, there's a verse, you probably remember it, that says, that the wife becomes pregnant,

00:34:54.000 --> 00:35:01.000
and the load becomes heavier and heavier, and then, they pray to God "please God, give us a good baby."

00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:07.000
And then, as soon as He gives them a good baby, they turn the baby into a god besides God.

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:09.000
Sura 7, very clear.

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:16.000
At the Sura 18, the person who lost his garden, his garden was his god. His property, his business, his job.

00:35:17.000 --> 00:35:21.000
The ego is another god, Sura 25.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:25.000
The ego can stop you from being saved.

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.000
The ego, NAFS (نفس).

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:41.000
So, in order, the Five Prayers, and this ZIKR (ذکر) will help you, as to who your god is.

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:45.000
The, the Creator of the heavens and earth will be your god through this ZIKR (ذکر).

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
It's a very important commandment.

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:51.000
(33:41) يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ ٱذْكُرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ ذِكْرًۭا كَثِيرًۭا

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:54.000
(33:42) وَسَبِّحُوهُ بُكْرَةًۭ وَأَصِيلًا

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:56.000
Make TASBIH (تسبیح) day and night.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Day and night, make TASBIH (تسبیح).

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.000
This is how we, this is how we get saved.

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:07.000
And then, when I asked you "who is your god?" and you might say "the Creator of the heavens and the earth", you will be right.

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:11.000
Only through this. Through ZIKR (ذکر).

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:19.000
As it is, when we examined ourselves, some time ago, and we discovered that we flunked,

00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:21.000
that the Creator of the heavens and the earth was not our god.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:24.000
We were preoccupied with other things.

00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:28.000
Then, we set the minimum, the minimum, of ZIKR (ذکر).

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.000
First thing in the morning, the Five Prayers.

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:36.000
You look at your child, and you say "Mã Shã Allãh", meaning, God gave you this... this is God's gift to me.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:41.000
And this immediately, invokes protection, for you and your child.

00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:45.000
There's a mechanism for it. It's very physical.

00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:50.000
Because when you say "Mã Shã Allãh", immediately, angels will guard your child.

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:56.000
Your child can go, ride the bicycle, and go between the traffic, and an (unintelligible)

00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:00.000
(unintelligible)

00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:05.000
But yes, your child will be protected, (unintelligible) anywhere.

00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:10.000
So, there's a mechanism for it when you say "Mã Shã Allãh."

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:13.000
So, IN SHAA ALLAH is a commandment.

00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:16.000
When we say "I'm gonna do" anything in the future, you must say "IN SHAA ALLAH."

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:17.000
Mã Shã Allãh.

00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:21.000
Subhan Allah. Anytime. Alhamdu Lillah.

00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:27.000
Oh, there is a commandment that says "do not eat from anything upon which the name of God was not pronounced."

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:34.000
And, although I tend to think this applies to meat, I think it applies to eggs, and peaches, and oranges.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:36.000
So, before you eat, say "Bismillah."

00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:40.000
Take that. Before you start anything, before you start your car, say "Bismillah."

00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:49.000
These, these are all just chances that we must grab to, to make God, our god,

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:52.000
and not our job, or our business, or our children, and so on.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:56.000
Cause this will give you everything else.

00:37:56.000 --> 00:38:02.000
This will guarantee you your job, it will guarantee you your children, it will guarantee you your spouse, and so on.

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:08.000
So, this is, I would say this, this opinion may be number one.

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:13.000
The Contact Prayers go a long way towards that.

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:18.000
Now, the idea behind all this is we don't want to repeat the mistake that we did in the past.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:22.000
Billions of years ago.

00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:23.000
We don't wanna be swept in the crowd.

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:27.000
It doesn't matter if the people around you do not do the Five Prayers. You do them.

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:36.000
And don't be, don't let Sheytan (Satan) tell you "oh, God should be happy that you do one Prayer." "I'm doing the Morning Prayer, so that should be enough. I'm better than all these people."

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:39.000
Yes, you are, but it's not enough.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:42.000
You're not giving yourself the, the proper meal.

00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:52.000
So, I think I will stop at this and let the questions or the discussions together remind me that we forgot anything.

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:57.000
And this is the basic idea as to why we are here.

00:38:57.000 --> 00:39:01.000
We thank God that He let us know first why we are here.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:05.000
He gave us a very sharp, clear picture to our generation.

00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:09.000
We wouldn't know this 20 years ago if we were born 20 years earlier.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:11.000
We wouldn't, we wouldn't know this.

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:14.000
God let us know that we were doing everything wrong.

00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:20.000
Everything we were doing, everything we grew up doing was wrong.

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:24.000
The NAMAZ (Salat) was wrong. The Zakat was wrong. The Fasting was wrong. The Hajj was wrong.

00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:27.000
We neglected the ZIKR (ذکر).

00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:32.000
And God, out of His mercy and grace, He taught us the correct way to do it.

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:43.000
So, we have to, right now, we should turn to God mentally and thank Him for showing us the right way,

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:48.000
and at the same time make a pledge that we will rejoin God's kingdom.

00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:51.000
(unintelligible) to ourselves.

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

