They were destroying NAMAZ (Salat) by mentioning the names of Muhammad, 'Al-e Muhammad, Ibrahim, 'Al-e Ibrahim in the Salat.

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:51.000
So, what is happening now is that God is purifying all these things for us. We must be devoted to God alone.

00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:57.000
But Sheytan (Satan) will always push somebody to be mentioned somebody next to God.

00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:05.000
In fact, the first pillar of Islam is gonna, the traditional five pillars, is what is called Shahadah.

00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:11.000
It is stated in the Quran as "La Elaha Ella Allah" or "Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah."

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:13.000
Sura 3, verse 18.

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:16.000
(3:18) شَهِدَ ٱللَّهُ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.000
This is the Shahadah.

00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:23.000
Now, when we grew up, they told us "the Shahadah is "Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wa Ash-hadu Anna Muhammadan Rasulallah."

00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:26.000
Now, this destroys the Shahadah.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:34.000
The first commandment in the Bible, the Old Testament, the New Testament, the Quran is "La Elaha Ella Allah."

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:38.000
When you add another name, it's not what Muhammad wants.

00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:41.000
It's what Sheytan (Satan) wants.

00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:50.000
And as a matter of fact, the Quran says that only the hypocrites will say "Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wa Ash-hadu Anna Muhammadan Rasulallah."

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:53.000
Dr. Khalifa: Go ahead.

00:41:54.000 --> 00:42:04.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's very good question. It's very good question. We did do this earlier today.

00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:18.000
In Sura 73, God says "commemorate God two-thirds of the night, one-third of the night, or one half of the night."

00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:19.000
It's all in the Sura.

00:42:19.000 --> 00:42:22.000
[73:3] ... little less. [73:4] Or a little more. ...

00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:26.000
Ok. Now, we have to understand that the night in the Quran begins at sunset.

00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:30.000
And also in the Torah, in all the scriptures.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:33.000
The night begins at sunset and ends at sunrise.

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:37.000
Now, if you do the Five Contact Prayers, you'll satisfy this requirement.

00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:40.000
Because you're gonna do the Sunset Prayer at 7 o'clock.

00:42:41.000 --> 00:42:44.000
You're gonna do the Night Prayer at 9 o'clock or 9:30.

00:42:45.000 --> 00:42:48.000
And you're gonna do the Dawn Prayer at 5 o'clock in the morning.

00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:54.000
So, from 7 to 10, that is 3 hours at the beginning of the night.

00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:58.000
And from 5 to 7, that's 2 hours in the morning.

00:42:59.000 --> 00:43:02.000
That's 5 hours, that's already 4:30 to 9:30.

00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:04.000
Almost half night.

00:43:05.000 --> 00:43:06.000
This is what it means.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:13.000
If you misunderstand it, you will get up in the middle of the night, and you will find yourself in a strange state.

00:43:14.000 --> 00:43:15.000
If you misunderstand it.

00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:17.000
But if you do the Five Prayers, you will...

00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:25.000
Also in addition to the Five Prayers, there is a strong recommendation in Sura 17 to read the Quran at dawn.

00:43:27.000 --> 00:43:31.000
So, you get up before sunrise, and you do the Morning Prayer, and read the Quran.

00:43:31.000 --> 00:43:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: And this will satisfy the requirement (unintelligible).

